[Music]  welcome to the QuickStart tutorial for  Cloud endpoints let's get started using  Cloud endpoints by activating the cloud  shell in our console we'll download the  project code to our instance if we take  a look at the scripts directory we'll  see that we've got a couple of scripts  in there let's start by running deploy  API Sh  this script will deploy an API included  in the project files to Cloud endpoints  next let's deploy the API back-end by  executing deploy app by Sh this will  create an app engine flexible  environment to host the API back-end and  deploy our sample API to App Engine to  see our API in action  we'll run query API sh this command  takes one argument a three-letter  Airport code for example if we answer a  WR our API returns Newark Liberty  International Airport cool  we've just deployed and tested an API  and endpoints once we have an API  deployed we can also track API activity  and gain insight into our users and  usage web stackdriver logging in order  to do that first let's enable the  service control API on our project  now let's generate some activity to work  with the generate traffic that Sh script  will generate requests to our API for  five minutes that will give us plenty of  data to check out metrics for once  traffic has been generated we can check  out the endpoint services page right off  the bat we've got visibility into the  number of requests per second 500 errors  and latency we can check out the logs  for the methods of our API through this  link at the bottom of the page we just  deployed our API and started generating  data so there aren't that many errors to  be seen but as you can see every request  to our API is logged with details like  timestamp of the request the method  called and the HTTP response code and  that's it that's how easy it is to get  setup with Cloud endpoints to deploy  your very own API  [Music]

